    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Nasim Nunez** emerges as our highest-rated asset at 62.09, benefitting significantly from a soft matchup against Feltner. While his #9 spot in the order acts as a drag on his run production, the combination of a favorable xERA (5.10) and his elite stolen base potential in a weak pitching environment makes him a priority start to pad our scarcest category. **Sam Antonacci** follows closely at 59.34; his leadoff role against Rocker provides a strong floor, and his ability to leverage the platoon advantage keeps his efficiency score firmly in the \"Strong\" start tier despite the moderate challenge of the opposing arm.\n\n**Jackson Merrill** (51.55) and **Miguel Vargas** (54.64) are functional, mid-tier plays today. While Merrill faces a tougher challenge against Ashcraft (3.28 xERA), his dynamic platoon profile keeps him relevant. The most difficult decision rested on **Tommy White** (55.05), who holds a strong park factor boost but suffers slightly from the R/R matchup against Matthews. He remains in the lineup over bench options like **Coby Mayo** or **Curtis Mead** due to his consistent recent output and superior projected RBI opportunities in the middle of the order. **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** are unfortunately sidelined by team off-days, forcing us to rely on our depth pieces like **Andy Pages** and **Heliot Ramos** to stabilize our output.\n\nWe are monitoring the weather closely, though no high-risk precipitation is currently flagged. The primary risk today is the inherent volatility of relying on players like **Nasim Nunez** for production at the bottom of the order, but given our need for speed, the projected volume remains too high to bench. We remain set with **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Josh Jung**, **Wade Meckler**, **Liam Hicks**, and **Luis Lara** in reserve, ready to rotate if lineup adjustments occur closer to first pitch. Focus today remains on efficiency: **Sam Antonacci** and **Nasim Nunez** are our best levers for moving the needle in a stagnant category.",
